      "notes": "All claims are adequately supported by their cited evidence. Tier assignments are appropriate: stated claims draw from policy text, measurable claims from sourced baselines, projected claims clearly flagged as uncertain. The direction 'improves' with 'minor' magnitude and 'low' confidence is well-justified by the rationale \u2014 the verdict does not overstate impact and explicitly flags the precedent problem with existing Covenant duties. No lever leakage: the verdict stays focused on O3 healthcare access effects. No party-blind issues detected. The mixed signals (existing services under-used, legal duties not reliably translating to delivered access) are cited on both sides appropriately, supporting the cautious 'improves/minor' rather than a false balance verdict. One minor note: E21 is from taylorwalton.co.uk (a law firm, commercial/media source) and is the sole basis for the 52%/60% claim \u2014 this should ideally be corroborated by an institutional source, but it is used only as a measurable baseline to contextualise need rather than to determine the verdict direction, so it does not rise to blocking."
